<SCENARIO VER="105">
{PLAYSND "SE\車走行中.ogg" "SE" "REPEAT" "0" "0"}
{CHGVOL "SE" "1000" "3000" "WAIT"}
{PLAYSND "togisuma.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
{WAIT "2000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{CREATECG "000" "グラフィック\背景\美冬車.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "R" "B" "0" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
{CREATECG "文字カウント画像" "グラフィック\システム\文字カウント画像.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "0" "1" "0" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
<TXSPN>The cherry blossoms of the dusk were in beautiful full bloom, bright against the clear sky.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Driving through it all felt pleasant.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Or so I would have thought, if it hadn't been this man beside me.<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"So, what's this about? Are you asking me on a date?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CREATECG "人物1" "グラフィック\立ち絵\人物\良治横顔逆.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "L" "B" "0" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="2">"............"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
In the passenger seat sat a <STYLE ID="2">Ryoji-san</STYLE> who said nothing at all.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
He had called me out, saying there was something important to talk about.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
When I suggested we go in my car to a place of my choosing, he agreed without any fuss.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{DELETECG "000,人物1" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0"}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{STOPSND "SE" "0" "PASS"}
{PLAYSND "SE\車エンジン切る.ogg" "VOICE" "NORMAL" "1000" "0"}
{WAITPLAY "VOICE" "CLICK"}
{MESON "500"}
The place we arrived at was that clearing on Mount Motoki.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
When I opened the window a little, chilly air crept in.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
This was where <STYLE ID="3">Eiichiro-san</STYLE> and I had eaten roasted sweet potatoes.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
But that stall was gone now.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CREATECG "000" "グラフィック\背景\美冬車.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "R" "B" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{CREATECG "人物1" "グラフィック\立ち絵\人物\良治横顔逆.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "L" "B" "0" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="1">"Well then, shall I hear what you have to say?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="2">"Yeah... right..."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="2">Ryoji-san</STYLE>, who had stayed silent all this while, spoke up.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "人物1" "グラフィック\立ち絵\人物\良治正面バストアップ.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "1000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
<STYLE ID="2">"</STYLE><STYLE ID="1">Mifuyu-san</STYLE><STYLE ID="2">, would you give </STYLE><STYLE ID="4">Haruka-chan</STYLE><STYLE ID="2"> back?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"............"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Nothing to be surprised about.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I'd had a feeling that someday I would hear something like that.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
The only other possibility would have been a request to stop watching them.<PG>
But that would mean separating <STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE> and <STYLE ID="5">Natsumi-chan</STYLE>.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Stopping the watching would mean living somewhere far away again―
{PAUSE ""}
in other words, I would have to put down roots in the Arata settlement.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE> and <STYLE ID="5">Natsumi-chan</STYLE> would be dead set against it, so, well, that was out too.<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"You're certainly blunt about it. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">I'm sure it's the result of a lot of talking with </STYLE><STYLE ID="6">Akane</STYLE><STYLE ID="1">."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="2">"............"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"What? Is that the end of your talk?</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">　If so, the answer's no. Adopted or not, you think I'd ever let go of </STYLE><STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE><STYLE ID="1">, who's dearer than anyone?</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">　Besides, how would you explain it to </STYLE><STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE><STYLE ID="1">?"</STYLE><PG>
Ridiculous.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
He was saying it knowing full well what my answer would be, so it struck me as nothing but comical.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I felt no anger and no sadness. It was simply, purely comical.<PG>
<STYLE ID="2">"I don't intend to explain everything to </STYLE><STYLE ID="4">Haruka-chan</STYLE><STYLE ID="2">. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="2">All I need to do is show the family register to </STYLE><STYLE ID="4">Haruka-chan</STYLE><STYLE ID="2"> and </STYLE><STYLE ID="5">Natsumi</STYLE><STYLE ID="2">."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Truly comical. Did he think <STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE> would leave me over that alone?
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE> would be 18 soon, after all.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I couldn't imagine her cutting her bond with me as parent and child over something that small.<PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"Ahahahaha! That's really too funny!</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">　I'd rather die than be separated from </STYLE><STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE><STYLE ID="1">! Ahahahaha!"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
As I cackled, <STYLE ID="2">Ryoji-san</STYLE> watched me steadily.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Did he still have something to say?<PG>
{STOPSND "BGM" "0" "PASS"}
<STYLE ID="2">"Then is it all right if I tell her there's a bug planted in her phone?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
If <STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE> found out about that, even her trust in me might well collapse.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"Ahaha, you just keep playing one card after another. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">I see, the bug. </STYLE>
{PLAYSND "見えない光_2.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
<STYLE ID="1">So, will you also tell her why the bug was planted?</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">　That </STYLE><STYLE ID="2">you</STYLE><STYLE ID="1"> two have killed six people so far, and that it was all for </STYLE><STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE><STYLE ID="1"> herself? </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">That's heavy for </STYLE><STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE><STYLE ID="1"> to carry. Ahahaha!"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="2">"If it comes to that, I will. It's about time we freed those two from our curse."</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"Haha..."</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="2">"............"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"............ </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">Are you serious?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="2">"Yeah. If you won't agree, </STYLE><STYLE ID="1">Mifuyu-san</STYLE><STYLE ID="2">, I intend to tell everything about what really happened in the Megasawa City case. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="2">If that happens, the investigation won't stop at you, </STYLE><STYLE ID="1">Mifuyu-san</STYLE><STYLE ID="2">. It'll reach even the Arata settlement."</STYLE><PG>
<STYLE ID="1">"If you do that... </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE><STYLE ID="1"> and </STYLE><STYLE ID="5">Natsumi-chan</STYLE><STYLE ID="1"> alike won't be able to live in this society. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">They'll have the </STYLE><STYLE ID="7" RUBY="らくいん">brand</STYLE><STYLE ID="1"> of daughters of the Megasawa City case killers </STYLE><STYLE ID="8" RUBY="お">stamped</STYLE><STYLE ID="1"> on them, won't they?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="2">"That's why I came to negotiate. I don't want to turn myself in either, if I can help it. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="4">Haruka-chan</STYLE><STYLE ID="2"> is all I want back."</STYLE><PG>
It didn't seem to be a bluff, either.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
If it came out, the three of us would be arrested as sick serial killers.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Then what would become of <STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE>?
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Society would look at her with curious eyes, and she might never be able to lead a normal life.<PG>
<STYLE ID="2">"Well? Won't you give </STYLE><STYLE ID="4">Haruka-chan</STYLE><STYLE ID="2"> back?"</STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I will never hand <STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE> over...!
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Rather than do that...!
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="1">"That was an amusing talk. Now, let's go back. </STYLE>
{PAUSE ""}
<STYLE ID="1">Or shall we really go on a date after this, behind </STYLE><STYLE ID="6">Akane</STYLE><STYLE ID="1">'s back?"</STYLE><PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{DELETECG "人物1" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0"}
{PLAYSND "SE\車室内エンジン.ogg" "VOICE" "NORMAL" "1000" "0"}
{PLAYSND "SE\車走行中.ogg" "SE" "REPEAT" "0" "0"}
{CHGVOL "SE" "1000" "3000" "WAIT"}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
―Feigning calm, I set the car moving.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Through the gap of the window I'd forgotten to close, cold air came in.<PG>
The moment the car started moving, <STYLE ID="2">Ryoji-san</STYLE> fell <STYLE ID="9" RUBY="つぐ">silent</STYLE> again.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
If I left things as they were, we would be arrested.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="2">Ryoji-san</STYLE> seemed prepared for that.<PG>
No, if it came to that, the brand of a murderer's daughter would follow <STYLE ID="5">Natsumi-chan</STYLE> around too.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
So it was a bluff after all...!
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
He could never do such a thing...!
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Inside, I breathed a sigh of <STYLE ID="10" RUBY="あんど">relief</STYLE>.<PG>
{STOPSND "BGM" "0" "PASS"}
{STOPSND "SE" "3000" "PASS"}
However, 
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
No... wait...<PG>
{PLAYSND "in_dream低.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
<STYLE ID="2">Ryoji-san</STYLE> couldn't think the negotiation would be settled by this one talk today, either.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
The negotiation was bound to go on.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Which meant there was no telling what card he would play next.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Even on the first day, he had played the bug card and the Megasawa City case card.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
He might bring out something even better at persuading me.<PG>
Just what card would he play?
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Abduct <STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE> by something close to kidnapping?
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
No, he might even kill me.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I could never, ever let go of <STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE>...!<PG>
That's right. <STYLE ID="2">Ryoji-san</STYLE> and his wife seemed to think they were the ones being watched, but the same went for me.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
We each shared the other's secrets, and each of us could use them to blackmail the other.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
So by now each of us was in the other's way, a threat to the other―
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
The best way, the way to cut this off, was for one side to disappear.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
From where I stood, it would be best for the Kogori family to disappear.<PG>
Tomorrow was April 8―<STYLE ID="3">Eiichiro-san</STYLE>'s thirteenth-year memorial service. [TN: Buddhist memorials count the year of death as the first year.]
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
If a fourth Megasawa City case were to happen, it could only be tomorrow.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
The place would be Motoki-cho, but as long as the date and the impact of the crime made their mark, I could make people think it was connected.<PG>
But that might also bring our crimes to light.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
In that case, should I take <STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE> to the Arata settlement, even by force...?
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
They would surely shelter us there.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE> was past 16 too, so she would be allowed to live in the Arata settlement.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
And if that failed, should I really die together with <STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE>...?<PG>
Even if I did it, there was no time, so I couldn't make a careful plan.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
First, I would erase <STYLE ID="2">this man</STYLE>.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
If I was to <STYLE ID="11" RUBY="なら">follow</STYLE> the methods of the past, I had to leave him in as gruesome a state as possible.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
And by a method that would kill him even if he was left alone.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Ideally with a weapon I could get even now―a method that needed only one knife...<PG>
―For a while, I recalled life in the Arata settlement.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Survival in the mountains, how to kill animals, how to butcher them―
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
All right. The best thing would be to make him a flayed body.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I had experience skinning creatures in the Arata settlement, and with a human the technique should be the same.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
It would take time, but I could still have him ready to be found tomorrow morning.<PG>
That left the place.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
This light car was too cramped, and outside, there was no telling who might see.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Somewhere no one would find me, a space all my own...<PG>
At this time of year, lots of minivans for setting up the food stalls were parked along the road near Central Park.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
If I could help myself to one, it would be better to do it inside.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Either way I was going to Arata or going to die. Stealing one car was no big deal.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Now, if I killed <STYLE ID="2">this man</STYLE> and the body was found, what would happen?<PG>
Tomorrow the crime would come to light, and school would be closed.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
During the past cases too, the schools in the area had closed the same way.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE> would probably spend the day with <STYLE ID="5">Natsumi-chan</STYLE>.<PG>
If I left those paper dolls on <STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE>'s desk, she would get uneasy and want to stay with <STYLE ID="5">Natsumi-chan</STYLE> all the more.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Good thing I had been giving <STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE> food poisoning practically every year.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I only needed to fool them for tomorrow, so it didn't have to be real <STYLE ID="12" RUBY="としゃぶつ">vomit</STYLE>.<PG>
With the bug, I could keep track of the two of them.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="5">Natsumi-chan</STYLE> and <STYLE ID="6">Akane</STYLE> might be called in by the police at some point, but it wouldn't be all night.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
And <STYLE ID="6">Akane</STYLE> would never confess to the past cases.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I would only have to lie in wait near the police station or at their home for them to come back.<PG>
The conditions were nicely in place.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Then, for when I killed <STYLE ID="5">Natsumi-chan</STYLE>, I would copy the shinigami's outfit and methods, so it wouldn't matter if <STYLE ID="4">Haruka</STYLE> saw me.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
During the day I would get together things to imitate the shinigami's outfit and weapon...
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I couldn't go to the memorial service tomorrow, but that hardly mattered anymore.<PG>
I should still have some of that drug in reserve.<PG>
